   "lines": [
    {
     "voice": "Reed (English (US))",
     "text": "Okay, thanks everyone for jumping on. This is the kickoff for the Epic Bill launch.",
     "file": "audio/r0_00.aiff",
     "duration": 5.615
    },
    {
     "voice": "Karen",
     "text": "Great. So first thing, we are not going to make Wednesday. I think we should move the launch to Friday.",
     "file": "audio/r0_01.aiff",
     "duration": 5.907
    },
    {
     "voice": "Reed (English (US))",
     "text": "Friday works. That gives us two more days for QA on the checkout flow.",
     "file": "audio/r0_02.aiff",
     "duration": 4.943
    },
    {
     "voice": "Daniel",
     "text": "On pricing, Kunal is going to own the pricing page. He has the new tiers and the annual discount.",
     "file": "audio/r0_03.aiff",
     "duration": 5.774
    },
    {
     "voice": "Karen",
     "text": "One risk. Refunds are still manual. We need Stripe webhooks wired up before we open the doors.",
     "file": "audio/r0_04.aiff",
     "duration": 5.641
    },
    {
     "voice": "Reed (English (US))",
     "text": "Agreed. Let's make the webhook work the top engineering priority this week.",
     "file": "audio/r0_05.aiff",
     "duration": 5.135
    },
    {
     "voice": "Daniel",
     "text": "And the onboarding emails are drafted, they just need a final pass.",
     "file": "audio/r0_06.aiff",
     "duration": 3.835
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "name": "Recording 2",
   "lines": [
    {
     "voice": "Karen",
     "text": "Quick follow up. Who actually signs off on the launch copy?",
     "file": "audio/r1_00.aiff",
     "duration": 3.48
    },
    {
     "voice": "Reed (English (US))",
     "text": "Let's say Pat has final sign off on copy, and legal reviews the refund language.",
     "file": "audio/r1_01.aiff",
     "duration": 5.486
    },
    {
     "voice": "Daniel",
     "text": "Perfect. I will send a recap and a Loom walkthrough by Monday.",
     "file": "audio/r1_02.aiff",
     "duration": 3.677
    },
    {
     "voice": "Karen",
     "text": "Sounds good. Talk Friday.",
     "file": "audio/r1_03.aiff",
